+# Bash background Stop cold settlement (toehold)
+
+Agent background Stop already persists Session `subagent_stop` entries and cold-recovers
+into `RuntimeTaskRegistry` without re-executing a child. Bash previously kept only a
+process-local `executionPort` map and memory-only `BackgroundTask*` events, so after
+restart Stop could not find settlement evidence and `backgroundWorks` went blank.
+
+## This toehold
+
+```text
+local_bash Stop settlement → Session entry type `bash_stop`
+live Bash/Agent/workflow BackgroundTaskCompleted emit → Session entry type `background_task_completed`
+live Bash/Agent BackgroundTaskStarted emit → Session entry type `background_task_started`
+cold reopen → restore terminal registry snapshot → Stop alreadyTerminal
+cold materialization → synthesize BackgroundTaskCompleted → backgroundWorks terminal
+  (Completed / bash_stop first; orphan Started → lost Completed)
+never restart a bash child
+never invent running works without live memory authority
+```
+
+- Writer (Stop): `stopLocalBashBackgroundTask` after cancel/lost settlement → `bash_stop`
+- Writer (live Completed): `persistDurableSessionEvent` on `BackgroundTaskCompleted` (bash + Agent/subagent + workflow)
+  → `background_task_completed`
+- Writer (live Started): `persistDurableSessionEvent` on `BackgroundTaskStarted` (bash + Agent/subagent)
+  → `background_task_started`
+- Reader (Stop): `resolveBackgroundStopTarget` via `recoverStoppedBashBackgroundTask`
+- Reader (projection): `loadPersistedConversationMaterialization` →
+  `projectColdBackgroundWorksEvents` (ordered registry
+  `COLD_BACKGROUND_WORKS_MATERIALIZATION_ORDER`: completed → bash_stop →
+  subagent_stop → orphan Started → lost). Individual synthesize helpers remain
+  the projector bodies; callers must not invent a shorter chain that skips
+  registry steps.
+- Proof: `bash-stop-recovery.test.ts` + `bash-stop-cold-projection.test.ts` +
+  `background-task-completed-durability.test.ts` +
+  `background-task-started-durability.test.ts` +
+  `agent-background-task-durability.test.ts` +
+  `cold-background-works-materialization.test.ts` (registry order)
+
+## Host claim authority
+
+Merged cold `backgroundWorks` claims, precedence, multi-source proof, registry
+order / per-`RuntimeTaskType` durability, and the shared non-claim list live in
+`host-cold-background-works-honesty.md`. This file keeps bash writers / Stop
+recovery detail only — it is not a second cold reconstruct authority and must
+not describe an incomplete chain versus the registry.
+
+`subagent_stop` cold projection is landed (sibling toehold); see the Host claim
+doc for the multi-source SQLite reopen proof.
