@@ -62,8 +62,37 @@ bounded transient rename succeeds once; Stop before rename publishes nothing; pe
 and symlink cases remain correct. Concurrent adapters and independent local processes with one
 observed revision produce one successful write and one `stale_write`, with lock cleanup/recovery.
 
+## Session shutdown and receipt lifetime
+
+Shutdown fences new ordinary inputs before admission and stops the current foreground through
+its existing cancellation owner. Accepted, undispatched ordinary FIFO inputs move to the existing
+Session input queue with their captured intent, model and attachments; their waiting callers receive
+cancellation after durable preservation. Shutdown never dispatches them. Cold recovery retains the
+existing interrupted-queue policy and does not replay uncertain work.
+
+App close starts owned executor/resource termination and waits for both the foreground command
+and runtime-owned residency work, including known late receipt publication. SQLite remains open
+through that settlement. Foreground Stop may finish before a mutating handler's late result;
+foreground idleness alone therefore does not permit closing the receipt writer.
+
+The existing six-second close deadline bounds acknowledgement, not receipt ownership. An expired
+deadline reports incomplete closure while the same App-owned cleanup and store remain alive until
+actual settlement. Repeated close calls share cleanup and resource effects; a later call can confirm
+the completed cleanup. No additional queue, journal, shutdown manager or storage owner is introduced.
+
+Acceptance: public Host/SQLite fixtures cover post-shutdown input refusal, preservation of accepted
+FIFO bindings through cold reopen, returned model usage during close, a no-foreground late tool
+receipt with exactly one file effect, repeated close, and deadline expiry followed by late settlement.
+
 Comparison: original ZCode `29628c9` stages then falls back to O_TRUNC on every failure. Current
 GenOffice retries rename but still uses direct fallback; Kun supplies a before-commit/Stop guard
 and optional fallback refusal. Adapt their bounded retry/fence ideas through Fleet's existing
 adapter and shared lock, and reject direct fallback. Exact source locks/evidence live in the root
 reference registry; no third-party implementation is copied or dependency added.
+
+Protocol shutdown also joins Apps whose factories began before shutdown. Outer cleanup keeps its
+existing 400 ms step / 1.2 s overall acknowledgement budgets; expiry reports incomplete shutdown
+and leaves one dependent cleanup chain awaiting actual App settlement before shared tools/SQLite
+close. A failed termination owner retains dependent resources and reports failure. These deferred
+promises survive only while the process lives; explicit forced exit/kill retains its existing
+budget and cannot promise later receipt persistence.
