diff --git a/packages/desktop/docs/fleet-packaging-identity.md b/packages/desktop/docs/fleet-packaging-identity.md
new file mode 100644
index 00000000..e5855411
--- /dev/null
+++ b/packages/desktop/docs/fleet-packaging-identity.md
@@ -0,0 +1,42 @@
+# Fleet packaging identity overlay (CORE-09)
+
+## Status
+
+Smallest reversible rebrand slice for the Fleet candidate (`.fleet/zcode`).
+
+- **Default brand:** `zcode` — existing `dev.zcode.app` / `ZCode` / `ZCode Preview` paths stay intact for local installs, CI, and any signed updater that still expects ZCode appId.
+- **Overlay:** `FLEET_PRODUCT_IDENTITY=1` switches electron-builder + compile-time desktop defines to Fleet product identity and strips z.ai commerce packaging metadata.
+- **About UI** already says Fleet; this overlay aligns **packaged** productName/appId/Linux package names/maintainer when explicitly enabled.
+
+## Enable
+
+```bash
+# Production-backend Fleet package identity (example; does not itself sign or publish)
+FLEET_PRODUCT_IDENTITY=1 ZCODE_ENV=production pnpm --dir packages/desktop exec node scripts/bundle.mjs --dry-run --os mac --arch arm64
+```
+
+Grammar matches `ZCODE_PREVIEW_IDENTITY`: only `1` enables; `0`/empty disables; any other value fails at build time.
+
+## Fleet identity table
+
+| Flavor | appId | productName | linux package |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| production | `dev.fleet.app` | Fleet | `fleet` |
+| preview | `dev.fleet.app.preview` | Fleet Preview | `fleet-preview` |
+
+Packaging metadata under Fleet brand uses RFC 2606 `.invalid` homepage/contact placeholders until a real Fleet support URL exists.
+
+## Blockers before making Fleet the default / distributing
+
+1. **Signed updater / feed** — no Fleet release channel yet; do not flip default appId while a production updater still targets ZCode identity.
+2. **Code signing / notarization secrets** — macOS `ZCODE_ENABLE_MAC_SIGN=1` still needs `APPLE_SIGNING_IDENTITY` / `CSC_NAME`; this overlay does not provision them.
+3. **Profile / keychain migration** — changing default appId or productName moves Electron userData; need an explicit migration plan for anyone who already ran ZCode-branded builds of this candidate.
+4. **Protocol scheme** — deep link scheme remains `zcode` for now (shared handler collision risk documented in electron-builder config).
+5. **Dev Electron copy** — `devElectronAppBundle.mjs` still stamps `ZCode Dev` / `dev.zcode.app.development` unless a follow-up wires the overlay there.
+6. **Homepage / support** — replace `https://fleet.invalid` and `noreply@fleet.invalid` before any public package.
+
+## Tests
+
+```bash
+node --test packages/desktop/scripts/desktop-product-identity.test.mjs
+```
